    Simple average:

    >>> x = jnp.array([1, 2, 3, 2, 4])
    >>> jnp.average(x)
    Array(2.4, dtype=float32)

    Weighted average:

    >>> weights = jnp.array([2, 1, 3, 2, 2])
    >>> jnp.average(x, weights=weights)
    Array(2.5, dtype=float32)

    Use ``returned=True`` to optionally return the normalization, i.e. the
    sum of weights:

